# Load path and tributary loads

The load path from the slab to the footing, drawn as a diagram, with the loads worked out at
each level.

```mermaid
graph LR
  Slab -->|w_s| Beam
  Beam -->|R_b| Column
  Column -->|N| Footing
  Footing -->|q| Soil
```

## Inputs
G: 4.5 kPa | slab dead load
Q: 3 kPa | slab live load
spacing: 3 m | beam spacing
L: 6 m | beam span
floors: 4 | storeys carried by the column

## Loads down the path
w_s: (1.2 * G + 1.5 * Q) * spacing -> kN/m | factored line load on a beam
R_b: w_s * L / 2 -> kN | beam end reaction
N: 2 * R_b * floors -> kN | column load (a beam on each side)

## Footing
B: 2 m | square footing width
q: N / B^2 -> kPa | bearing pressure under the footing
